name issue_464_start_rate_above_int_bps
describe The host configures a 20 Gbps start rate and a 9 Ebps max; the call settles on the 2.5 Mbps link as with libwebrtc's largest configurable rate (INT_MAX bps)
# Issue #464: libwebrtc's BitrateConstraints carry int bps (call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc:68-83,
# ConvertConstraints), so a host can't configure a finite rate above INT_MAX bps (about 2.1 Gbps).
# GccController took any DataRate: at a start rate of 1 Tbps or more the 3x and 6x start probes made
# the pacer build padding for petabit bursts (RtpSender::GeneratePadding) until std::bad_alloc, and at
# 20 Gbps the call never settled (9-14 freezes, cc.unsettled 1 on seeds 1-5). cc::ConvertConstraints
# now saturates the min, start and max rate at INT_MAX bps (src/cc/send_side_bwe.cc). 20 Gbps keeps
# the base commit's run short; any start rate above INT_MAX bps now gives these same results.
duration 10s
max_rate 9000000000000mbps
start_rate 20000mbps
# compare_seeds 40 (#777): video.longest_freeze_ms reads 561 vs libwebrtc 441 (band 100) after #775,
# behind on 2/10 seeds; ours spans to 1140-1205 ms on seeds 11-40 and libwebrtc's seeds 1-10 to 627.
# Ten seeds can't tell spread from a gap; 40 seeds on both stacks settle it.
compare_seeds 40
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=400ms
expect cc.unsettled == 0
expect cc.max_settle_ms <= 2000
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect video.freeze_count <= 1
expect video.longest_freeze_ms <= 1000
